{
 "points": [
  {
   "id": "P1.1",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Limited novelty: combines sharpness-aware optimization with MTT with minor optimization changes.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.2",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No comparison with other methods incorporating sharpness-aware minimization.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.3",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Missing recent SOTA baselines such as RDED, NRR-DD, SRe2L.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.1",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Missing decoupled, diffusion-based and optimization-free distillation baselines (SRe2L, RDED, DELT, etc.).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.2",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Experiments limited to ConvNet; no VGG, ResNet or ViT.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.3",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Generalization accuracy improvements in Table 2 marginal (often below 1%).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.4",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "No ablation of trajectory reusing and TUH approximations.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.5",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Runtime cost relative to TESLA high despite modest gains, weakening efficiency argument.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P3.1",
   "reviewer": "P3",
   "text": "Several hyperparameters need careful tuning; setup and transferability to other datasets/architectures unclear.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P3.2",
   "reviewer": "P3",
   "text": "Lacks discussion of related works on sharpness/generality and dataset bias in distillation.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.1",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Limited novelty: simple SAM application; truncated unrolling similar to k-step SGD.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.2",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Improvement over SOTA methods incremental.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.3",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Missing latest efficient distillation SOTA methods (KRR, M3D, model augmentation).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.1",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "In-domain gains versus FTD marginal, within std, sometimes negative; 'noticeable margins' overstated.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.2",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No significance testing; number of seeds unclear.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.3",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No ablation separating SAM perturbation, input noise, TUH, TR and learning-rate rule.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.4",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No sensitivity analysis for rho, gamma, tau, iota.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.5",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Why pixel-space flatness of synthetic data improves generalization is not argued.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.6",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Fig. 2 gradient-norm evidence does not show flatter minima; no common sharpness or Hessian analysis.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.7",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Prop. 4.1 convergence/strong convexity assumptions do not hold in practical non-convex short-trajectory setting.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.8",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Confusing notation for iota and inconsistent bound factors.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.9",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Thm. 4.2 bound loose, depends on unspecified learning rate, not numerically checked.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.10",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Smoothness and continuity assumptions imprecisely stated.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.11",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Claims of rigorous theoretical support overstated.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.12",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Learning-rate update described only qualitatively; second-order comparison deferred to appendix.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.13",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Table 8 shows extreme sensitivity to retained truncation fraction (27-point swing).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.14",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Text describing Table 8 trend contradicts the table.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.15",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Truncation knob apparently tuned per dataset; unclear if baselines tuned comparably.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.16",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Memory claim overstated: SATM uses more memory than TESLA.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.17",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Runtime advantages over MTT/TESLA negligible.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.18",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Efficiency reporting inconsistent: identical ImageNet memory, two-GPU remark, complexity vs faster claim.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.19",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "ImageNet-1K claims rest only on TESLA comparison with small gains.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.20",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No comparison with modern ImageNet-scale methods like SRe2L and RDED.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.21",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Unclear whether TESLA numbers use soft labels; comparison possibly unequal.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.22",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "ImageNet subset results compare only to MTT and FTD.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.23",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Recent trajectory-matching methods such as DATM absent from main tables.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.24",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "SATM-DA add-on results mixed with overlapping standard deviations.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.25",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "MTT numbers inconsistent across tables without reconciliation.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.26",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Continual learning compares few baselines with curves only, no numbers or variance.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.27",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Several typos.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.28",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Novelty limited: direct transplant of SAM to data; engineering contributions incremental.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.29",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Noise scaled by data norm motivated only by citations, without analysis.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.30",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Trajectory reuse means hypergradient not at perturbed point; 'sharpness-aware' label questionable.",
   "minor": false
  }
